Subject: [PATCH] libunwind: define the __cpp_exception tag on wasm

Backport of llvm/llvm-project#185770 ([WebAssembly] Move __cpp_exception to
libunwind). `_Unwind_RaiseException` calls `__builtin_wasm_throw(0, ...)`,
which references the `__cpp_exception` tag; without a definition the wasm64
libunwind build leaves it undefined at link time.

Needed when building libunwind/libc++abi/libc++ for wasm64-wasip1 out of
contrib/llvm-project/runtimes (see cmake/wasi/STATUS.md).

diff --git a/libunwind/src/Unwind-wasm.c b/libunwind/src/Unwind-wasm.c
index b0d6cd2d0..b0a14f68b 100644
--- a/libunwind/src/Unwind-wasm.c
+++ b/libunwind/src/Unwind-wasm.c
@@ -69,6 +69,19 @@ _Unwind_RaiseException(_Unwind_Exception *exception_object) {
   __builtin_wasm_throw(0, exception_object);
 }
 
+// Backport of llvm/llvm-project#185770 ([WebAssembly] Move __cpp_exception to
+// libunwind): define the `__cpp_exception` tag which `__builtin_wasm_throw`
+// above references, as the single canonical definition for this API.
+__asm__(".globl __cpp_exception\n"
+#if defined(__wasm32__)
+        ".tagtype __cpp_exception i32\n"
+#elif defined(__wasm64__)
+        ".tagtype __cpp_exception i64\n"
+#else
+#error "Unsupported Wasm architecture"
+#endif
+        "__cpp_exception:\n");
+
 /// Called by __cxa_end_catch.
 _LIBUNWIND_EXPORT void
 _Unwind_DeleteException(_Unwind_Exception *exception_object) {
